# Only this project's exclusions. Everything else is published, including
# every .m and .py file in code/.


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
#  The Umbra scenes
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
#  3.08 GB across 9 GeoTIFFs. Six are over GitHub's 100 MB hard file
#  limit, the largest 570 MB. They are public, so the README gives the
#  names and the download link instead of re-hosting them:
#
#      Umbra Open Data, CC BY 4.0
#      https://umbra.space/open-data
#
#  Everything derived from them IS published, so the work reproduces
#  without the 3 GB: data/previews/ and data/crops/.
#
data/raw/


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
#  Working material, kept locally and not published
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
/paper/
_quarantine_2026-10-12/


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
#  MATLAB Project metadata
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
#  83 machine-generated XML files that only the MATLAB Project feature
#  reads. No script in this repository uses it. The MATLAB code itself,
#  every .m file in code/ and code/figures_code/, is published.
#
code/resources/
code/src.prj


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
#  Published on purpose, listed so nothing excludes them later
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
#      code/*.m              the 15 MATLAB scripts and the library
#      code/figures_code/    the 7 figure scripts
#      code/*.py             the 4 Python tools
#      code/results_*.csv    the regression gate's baseline. A missing
#                            baseline is a hard failure, not a skip
#      data/crops.csv        the crop definitions
#      data/crops/           globbed by real_calibrate_neg.m,
#                            real_channels.m, real_detect.m and
#                            refine_calib.py
#      data/previews/        one preview image per scene
#      data/simulated/       the saved test images the figures are
#                            redrawn from, with no new random numbers
#      results/tables/       the 19 frozen CSVs every reported number
#                            is taken from
